    "author": "CookingwithRia",
    "ingredients": [
      "2 cups all-purpose flour",
      "4 teaspoons baking powder, aluminum free",
      "1/4 teaspoon baking soda",
      "3 tbs granulated sugar",
      "1 teaspoon Himalayan salt",
      "1 stick butter, 4 oz, 1/2 cup, cold or semi frozen",
      "1 cup buttermilk, full fat, cold"
    ],
    "description": "Buttermilk biscuits, my go-to quick dessert on a cold winter weekend night, made with flour, cold butter, buttermilk and a few pantry staples. No buttermilk? Vinegar and whole milk work too.",
    "instructions": [
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Preheat oven to 400F."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "In a bowl combine flour, sugar, baking powder and baking soda."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "In a food processor fitted with the grater attachment or using a grater, grate butter."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Add grated butter to the flour mixture (you can also do this in the food processor) and rub in (or pulse) to combine until it forms crumbs."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Gradually add buttermilk and squeeze together to make a soft and sticky dough. Do not knead."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Place dough on a lightly floured counter. Flatten into a square and fold one end towards the middle, fold the other side over the entire dough to allow the edges to meet. Rotate horizontally and repeat a total of 4 times."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Flatten out until 1/2 inch thick and using a 2 inch pastry cutter, cut into 10-12 pieces. Place on a buttered cast iron pan or narrow tray. Ensure that they are close together to allow them to rise instead of spreading out. Brush with buttermilk."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Place in a preheated oven and bake for 12-15 minutes or until fully risen, cooked and the top is golden brown."
      }
    ],
