    "description": "Caribbean coo coo (cou cou), the way my Nani made it: fine cornmeal cooked with coconut milk, ochro, garlic, thyme and fresh seasonings until smooth, then cut into squares.",
    "instructions": [
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "If using fresh or frozen grated coconut, add 14 oz coconut to the mug of a blender with 5 cups hot water. Pulse for 1 minute and strain. If using blocked coconut cream or coconut powder, boil or mix with 5 cups water, or according to package instructions. If using canned coconut milk, mix with enough water to make 5 cups."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Mix 1 cup cornmeal with two and a half cups coconut milk or enough to make a runny consistency. As you allow it to sit it absorbs the water, so mix right before adding to the pot. Set aside."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "In a medium saucepan over medium heat, heat oil and butter, add the ochro, scallion, onion, garlic, hot or pimento pepper and thyme and cook for 3 mins. Add the remainder of the coconut milk(2.5 cups), salt and sugar, if using."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Bring to a boil, reduce heat to low and simmer for 5-7 minutes."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Gradually add cornmeal to milk, stirring constantly with a wooden spoon. Stir in butter. Cook, in a whisking motion for 5-10 minutes or until it thickens and comes away from the sides of the pot. Pour into a prepared glass baking dish, smoothen with a spatula and cool."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Cut into pieces and serve."
      }
    ],
