    "description": "Tender lauki is simmered in a fragrant curry until it releases its own juices, then seasoned shrimp is added near the end so it remains tender. Omit the shrimp for an easy vegetarian or vegan curry lauki.",
    "instructions": [
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Prepare and season the shrimp – Peel and devein the shrimp, then cut each into 3 to 4 pieces depending on size. Season with 2 tablespoons green seasoning, 1 teaspoon salt, 1 teaspoon black pepper, 1 tablespoon minced garlic and 1 teaspoon thyme leaves. Mix well and set aside. If using whole thyme sprigs instead, reserve them for the lauki."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Prepare the lauki: Wash and peel the lauki, then cut into very small cubes."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Temper the spices and brown the onion: Heat the extra virgin olive oil in a 5-quart pot over medium-high heat. Add the sliced onion, hot pepper, curry leaves and optional panch phoron. If substituting, add a pinch each of methi seeds and whole cumin seeds. Cook until the edges of the onion are browned."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Cook the curry: Add the curry powder, turmeric, remaining 2 tablespoons green seasoning, remaining 1 tablespoon minced garlic and chopped tomatoes. Mix well. Add ½ cup water and cook, stirring, for 3 to 5 minutes, until the curry is fragrant and grainy and begins separating from the oil."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Add the lauki: Add the cubed lauki and about 1 tablespoon salt, or to taste. If using thyme sprigs, add them now. Mix thoroughly and cook for about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally to bring everything back up to temperature."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Cover and cook the lauki: Cover, reduce the heat to medium-low and allow the lauki to simmer in the liquid it releases. Check and stir approximately every 5 minutes to make sure it does not stick."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Cook until tender – approximately 20 minutes: Continue cooking until the lauki is tender and there is still some liquid in the pot. Cooking time varies. If the lauki softens and begins breaking down sooner, proceed to the shrimp. Firmer lauki may require 20 minutes or longer."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Add the shrimp : Stir in the seasoned shrimp. Raise the heat to high and bring the curry back to a bubble."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Finish cooking: Reduce the heat to low, cover and cook for 10 to 15 minutes, or until the shrimp is fully cooked and the sauce has thickened. Avoid extending the cooking time unnecessarily."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Taste and finish: Taste and add more salt if required. Stir in the ground roasted cumin and chopped culantro or cilantro. Remove thyme sprigs, if used, and serve."
      }
    ],
    "yields": 8,
    "prepTime": "PT20M",
    "cookTime": "PT45M",
    "totalTime": "PT1H5M",
    "image": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Elephant_Foot_Yam_Curry_with_Shrimps-_Amorphophallus_paeoniifolius.jpg/960px-Elephant_Foot_Yam_Curry_with_Shrimps-_Amorphophallus_paeoniifolius.jpg",
    "imageCredit": "Aseedtolife (CC BY-SA 4.0) via Wikimedia Commons"
