        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Fill a large bowl with water, add beans and soak beans overnight. Next day rinse and drain. Fill 12 cups water in a stock pot and bring to a boil. Add beans and cover ajar, reduce heat to a simmer and cook for 1 hour or until tender but firm. When cool. Separate beans from the liquid. Set aside."
