    "id": "carib-trinidad-tobago-shepherds-pie",
    "country": "Trinidad & Tobago",
    "name": "Shepherd’s Pie",
    "source": "Cooking with Ria",
    "sourceUrl": "https://cookingwithria.com/2022/11/shepherds-pie/",
    "author": "CookingwithRia",
    "ingredients": [
      "2 lbs potatoes",
      "1 clove garlic",
      "1 egg, whisked",
      "1 cup heavy cream, warm (or evaporated or whole milk)",
      "6 tbs butter, room temp",
      "Salt, to taste",
      "4 tbs extra virgin olive oil",
      "1 onion, Chopped",
      "2 lbs ground lamb",
      "1 tbs green seasoning",
      "1 celery, chopped",
      "1 scallion, chopped",
      "1 tbs minced garlic",
      "1 red bell pepper, chopped",
      "Hot Pepper",
      "1 bay leaf",
      "2 tsp salt",
      "1 tsp black pepper",
      "1 tsp onion flakes",
      "1 tsp dried oregano",
      "1 tsp crushed red pepper",
      "8 ozs peas and carrots",
      "4 tbs tomato paste, optional"
    ],
    "description": "Shepherd's pie, one of my favorite comfort foods: ground lamb cooked with green seasoning, herbs, peas and carrots, topped with creamy garlic mashed potatoes and baked until golden.",
    "instructions": [
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Peel, rinse, quarter and place potatoes in a medium pot, cover with water and add 1 tbs salt and garlic. Bring to a boil, lower heat to medium high and cook until fork glides easily through the potato. If undercooked there will be lumps in the mashed potato so it is important to get this right. Drain."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Place back into the pot it was cooked in. Immediately add boiled garlic, egg and butter and whisk and mash with a fork to combine. Gradually add warm cream and continue to whisk until creamy, light and fluffy. You can also use a handheld mixer to whisk."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Add salt to taste. Set aside"
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "In a medium heavy bottomed pot, heat oil. Add onion and cook until the edges are golden brown."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Add meat and using a wooden spoon, break up any chunks. Cook the ground meat until it’s no longer pink, about 5 minutes. Add in the remaining ingredients, green seasoning, celery, scallion, garlic, bell, pepper, hot pepper, bayleaf. Mix well to combine, cleaning down the sides of the pot."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Stir in salt, black pepper, granulated onion, oregano and pepper flakes. Taste and adjust as necessary. Pour in the peas and carrots, stir well to combine. Cover and cook for 10 minutes to allow the flavors to meld together."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "To assemble, place the meat onto the bottom of a baking dish 7 x 11. Spread the mashed potato on top of the cooked lamb. Place in a preheated oven for 20-30 minutes or until the top is golden brown."
      }
    ],
    "yields": 10,
    "prepTime": "PT30M",
    "cookTime": "PT30M",
    "totalTime": "PT1H",
    "image": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Homerton_College_-_Shepherd%27s_pie.jpg/960px-Homerton_College_-_Shepherd%27s_pie.jpg",
    "imageCredit": "Oxfordian Kissuth (CC BY-SA 3.0) via Wikimedia Commons"
