    "name": "Spicy Pickled Red Onion",
    "source": "Cooking with Ria",
    "sourceUrl": "https://cookingwithria.com/2026/02/spicy-pickled-red-onion/",
    "author": "CookingwithRia",
    "ingredients": [
      "medium red onion, peeled and sliced (not too thin, not too thick)",
      "1 head garlic, peeled and thinly sliced or finely chopped, or amount per your reference",
      "6 large sprigs parsley, hard stems removed, leaves finely chopped",
      "Hot pepper, to taste (finely chopped)",
      "Juice of 2 limes, or use white vinegar, or a mix of lime + vinegar",
      "Salt, to taste",
      "Black pepper, to taste"
    ],
    "description": "This spicy pickled red onion is a quick, fresh condiment made with lime (or vinegar), garlic, parsley, and hot pepper. It’s bright, sharp, and best enjoyed within 2–3 days.",
    "instructions": [
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Slice the onion: Peel and slice the red onion with a knife or mandolin, keeping slices not too thin and not too thick so they soften without turning limp."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Prepare the garlic: Peel the garlic and slice thinly, or chop finely if you prefer it to blend into the condiment."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Chop the parsley: Remove the hard stems and finely chop the parsley leaves only."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Prepare the hot pepper: Remove the stem and chop finely. For a less invasive heat, remove the seeds before chopping."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Add the acid: Squeeze the juice of two limes into the bowl, catching seeds as you go. If using vinegar, add it here instead, or combine vinegar and lime juice."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Season and mix: Add salt and black pepper, then mix well until everything is coated and evenly distributed."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Jar and refrigerate: Spoon into a sterilized glass jar or mason jar, seal, and refrigerate."
      }
    ],
