    "sourceUrl": "https://cookingwithria.com/2011/04/super-sunday-french-toast/",
    "author": "CookingwithRia",
    "ingredients": [
      "1 cup whole milk or evaporated milk",
      "4 large eggs",
      "1-2 tablespoons brown sugar, maple syrup or honey, optional",
      "1-2 teaspoons ground cinnamon",
      "salt, to taste, about 1/2 teaspoon (optional)",
      "6-8 slices day-old bread, about 1/2 inch each (brioche, challah, whole grain)",
      "butter, for frying"
    ],
    "description": "Easy, fluffy French toast with cinnamon, made with day-old brioche, challah or whole grain bread. Serve with butter, maple syrup or honey and fresh fruit.",
    "instructions": [
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Slice the bread. Cut the bread about ½ inch thick. For French toast sticks, cut each slice into three strips lengthwise."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Make the mixture. In a shallow bowl, add the eggs, milk, sweetener, salt and cinnamon. Whisk until blended. This is a great step for little helpers."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Soak. Dip the bread into the egg mixture and let it soak up some of the mixture. Flip and repeat. Do not leave it in too long or it will get soggy and start to break apart."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Fry. Melt butter in a large skillet or griddle over medium-high heat. Add the soaked bread without crowding the pan and fry until brown on both sides and fully cooked, about 2 to 3 minutes per side. It fluffs up when it is done."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Repeat. Repeat with the remaining bread and egg mixture, frying in batches and adding a little more butter for each batch."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "Serve. Serve with butter, maple syrup or honey and fresh fruit."
      }
    ],
    "yields": 4,
    "prepTime": "PT10M",
    "cookTime": "PT15M",
    "totalTime": "PT25M",
